From: Shreenidhi Shedi <shreenidhi.shedi@broadcom.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] sandbox: allow recvmsg, sendmsg, rseq, membarrier syscalls

RCA
---
OpenSSH 10.5 split the preauth code into a separately re-executed binary
(sshd-auth). The seccomp sandbox is installed in sshd-auth before kex
begins (sshd-auth.c: ssh_sandbox_child() at line 213, do_ssh2_kex() at
line 735). After receiving SSH2_MSG_KEXECDH_INIT the kex handler calls
mm_receive_fd() in monitor_fdpass.c to pull a file descriptor from the
sshd-session monitor via SCM_RIGHTS. This uses recvmsg(2) (NR 47 on
x86_64), which was not in the seccomp allowlist. The sandbox default
action is SECCOMP_RET_KILL, so sshd-auth was killed with SIGSYS before
it could complete the handshake.

The PQC patches replaced libcrux ML-KEM with OpenSSL EVP.
The EVP code path for ML-KEM goes through a kex handler branch that
reaches mm_receive_fd(), whereas the libcrux path did not. The sandbox
allowlist was never updated to cover this new code path.

Additionally, glibc 2.35+ registers threads with rseq(2) (NR 334) and
uses membarrier(2) (NR 324) during CRYPTO_THREAD_run_once() called by
EVP provider initialisation. Both were also absent from the allowlist.

Fix: add SC_ALLOW entries for recvmsg, sendmsg (the paired send side),
rseq, and membarrier.

Signed-off-by: Shreenidhi Shedi <shreenidhi.shedi@broadcom.com>
---
 sandbox-seccomp-filter.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sandbox-seccomp-filter.c b/sandbox-seccomp-filter.c
index xxxxxxx..xxxxxxx 100644
--- a/sandbox-seccomp-filter.c
+++ b/sandbox-seccomp-filter.c
@@ -323,6 +323,12 @@
 #ifdef __NR_getpid
 	SC_ALLOW(__NR_getpid),
 #endif
+#ifdef __NR_rseq
+	SC_ALLOW(__NR_rseq),
+#endif
+#ifdef __NR_membarrier
+	SC_ALLOW(__NR_membarrier),
+#endif
 #ifdef __NR_getrandom
 	SC_ALLOW(__NR_getrandom),
 #endif
@@ -426,6 +432,13 @@
 #ifdef __NR_writev
 	SC_ALLOW(__NR_writev),
 #endif
+#ifdef __NR_recvmsg
+	/* needed for monitor fd-passing (SCM_RIGHTS) during kex signing */
+	SC_ALLOW(__NR_recvmsg),
+#endif
+#ifdef __NR_sendmsg
+	SC_ALLOW(__NR_sendmsg),
+#endif
 #ifdef __NR_getsockopt
 	SC_ALLOW(__NR_getsockopt),
 #endif
